_to_tree`, or takes bytes not str — index/tools code fails to import or mis-parses, and the plan's meta-extraction (line ranges from `Tree.meta`) breaks silently.","propagate_positions default differs, so JSON key ranges / line ranges required by the receipt and lookup_declaration cannot be produced."],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Attach the verbatim `python -c` probe output (interpreter version, `hcl2.__version__`, `inspect.signature`, and a sample `Tree.meta`) to the leaf ticket and reference that comment id directly in the plan; if the symbol is `parse_to_tree`/bytes-based, correct the plan's signature and the 'decode to str' step accordingly.","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"no","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"no","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"broken_oracle","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"certification_cannot_prove","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"high","reversibility":"moderate","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Specify that module/file/byte bounds are checked INCREMENTALLY during closure expansion (abort and abstain the moment a running count crosses a limit), not only after the full closure is materialized, so a pathological repo cannot exhaust the worker before the limit fires.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.534,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan: 'Index affected directories; follow repo-contained literal children/reverse callers' then 'Enforce 64 modules, 5,000 files, 32 MiB, and the existing 60-second deadline before returning facts; any failure yields one abstention with no partial facts.'","The ordering implies enforcement AFTER building the closure; only the 60s worker deadline (harness.py _DEFAULT_TIMEOUT) bounds wall-clock, not memory/handles consumed during expansion.","harness.run_in_worker bounds a hang/segfault but does not cap the worker's own memory/IO growth."],"finding":"The resource bounds (64 modules, 5,000 files, 32 MiB) are specified as enforced 'before returning facts' — i.e. after the closure is built — but the plan does not state that byte/file/module counts are checked INCREMENTALLY during closure expansion (following literal children/reverse callers and reading file bytes). Only the 60-second deadline backstops runtime; nothing bounds bytes or file handles consumed while the index is being built. A pathological repo could read far past 32 MiB / 5,000 files before the post-hoc check trips.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f2bc273df0419a9f8","impact":0.264,"is_primary":null,"location":"Scope → Structural index (bounds bullet: 'Enforce 64 modules, 5,000 files, 32 MiB, and the existing 60-second deadline before returning facts')","norm_id":"nb88fba6a006612b0","priority":0.066,"reason":"low-validity","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A repo whose bounded closure crosses many directories and large .tf.json files reads gigabytes of bytes into the worker before the 32 MiB check runs, risking OOM/kill (which surfaces as parse_error, not the intended byte_limit abstention).","A monorepo with thousands of .tf files under one affected module tree is fully enumerated before the 5,000-file limit is applied."],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"State that the index accumulates module/file/byte counters as it discovers each directory/child/caller and reads bytes, and abstains (other/module_limit|file_limit|byte_limit) at the first crossing — before reading the offending file's remaining bytes — so bounds are a guard on the traversal, not a post-hoc audit of a fully-built closure.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.25,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"no","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"low"}}},{"block_threshold":0.9,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Re-anchor the python-hcl2 8.1.3 surface evidence to a comment/artifact that actually contains the import-probe command and output (confirming the exact entry point — parses_to_tree vs parse_to_tree — its str/bytes signature, lark Tree return, propagate_positions, and serialized meta keys against the installed 8.1.3 wheel), and correct the cited date/location in the plan.","cohort":["T3"],"criteria":["T3"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":0.1,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan quote: 'parses_to_tree signature (text: str) -> lark.tree.Tree; parser().options.propagate_positions=True; Tree.meta block (1,1,3,2), attribute (2,2,2,15); serialized meta keys [\"__is_block__\"]'","Plan quote: '